# CareerUp — Simplified Data Dictionary

This dictionary describes the current 12-table core ERD.

Data types, lengths, defaults, and status values below are proposed
implementation choices for team confirmation. No database is implemented
by this document.

## Legend

- PK: Primary key — uniquely identifies a record.
- FK: Foreign key — references a record in another table.
- UQ: Unique constraint — prevents duplicates.
- Required: The field cannot be NULL.
- Optional: The field may be NULL.
- Composite key: Two fields form one key together.

All ID fields and their referencing foreign keys use INT UNSIGNED.

## 1. USERS

Stores accounts and basic profile information for all roles.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| user_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique account ID. |
| company_id | INT UNSIGNED | No | FK | References COMPANIES.company_id; optional employer affiliation. |
| name | VARCHAR(100) | Yes | — | User's displayed name. |
| email | VARCHAR(254) | Yes | UQ | Unique sign-in email address. |
| password_hash | VARCHAR(255) | Yes | — | Password hash; never a plain-text password. |
| role | VARCHAR(30) | Yes | — | Student, Recruiter, Company Representative, Career Advisor, or Administrator. |
| school | VARCHAR(150) | No | — | School affiliation. |
| major | VARCHAR(100) | No | — | Student's academic major. |
| graduation_year | SMALLINT UNSIGNED | No | — | Expected or completed graduation year. |
| bio | TEXT | No | — | Professional biography. |

A user has one role and at most one company affiliation in this design.
Role-specific profile requirements must be checked by the application.

## 2. COMPANIES

Stores employer information.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| company_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique employer ID. |
| name | VARCHAR(150) | Yes | — | Company name; not assumed globally unique. |
| industry | VARCHAR(100) | No | — | Employer's industry. |
| description | TEXT | No | — | Company introduction or culture information. |
| website | VARCHAR(500) | No | — | Company website address. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: PENDING, APPROVED, or INACTIVE. |

A company may have many affiliated users, opportunities, and
collaboration requests.

## 3. POSTS

Stores content displayed in portfolios and the discovery feed.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| post_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique post ID. |
| author_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References USERS.user_id; identifies the creator. |
| title | VARCHAR(150) | Yes | — | Project or accomplishment title. |
| description | TEXT | No | — | Explanation of the work. |
| created_at | DATETIME | Yes | — | Creation time; supports feed sorting. |
| category | VARCHAR(100) | No | — | Academic or project category. |
| visibility | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: PUBLIC or PRIVATE. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: DRAFT, PUBLISHED, or ARCHIVED. |

Each post has exactly one author. An author may create many posts.
The portfolio and feed reuse the same post rather than duplicate it.

## 4. POST_MEDIA

Stores multiple image or video references for a post.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| media_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique media ID. |
| post_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References POSTS.post_id. |
| media_url | VARCHAR(1000) | Yes | — | Location of the uploaded media. |
| media_type | VARCHAR(10) | Yes | — | Proposed: IMAGE or VIDEO. |
| display_order | SMALLINT UNSIGNED | Yes | UQ pair | Positive position within the post. |

The combination (post_id, display_order) must be unique.

Each media record belongs to one post. A draft may have no media;
the application must require at least one valid media item before
publishing a media post.

The database stores the media reference, not the uploaded file bytes.

## 5. SKILLS

Stores standardized skill names.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| skill_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique skill ID. |
| name | VARCHAR(100) | Yes | UQ | Unique skill name, such as Java or Graphic Design. |
| active | BOOLEAN | Yes | — | Whether the skill is available for selection. |

Proposed default for active: TRUE.

A skill can be associated with many profiles and posts.

## 6. USER_SKILLS

Connects users to their profile skills.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| user_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References USERS.user_id. |
| skill_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References SKILLS.skill_id. |

Composite primary key: (user_id, skill_id).

A user can have multiple skills, and a skill can belong to multiple
users. The composite key prevents the same pairing appearing twice.

## 7. POST_SKILLS

Connects portfolio posts to skill tags.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| post_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References POSTS.post_id. |
| skill_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References SKILLS.skill_id. |

Composite primary key: (post_id, skill_id).

A post can have multiple skill tags. The composite key prevents
the same skill being attached to the same post twice.

## 8. COLLABORATIONS

Stores a student's request for company verification of their own post.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| collaboration_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique verification request ID. |
| post_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK + UQ | References POSTS.post_id. |
| student_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References USERS.user_id; must match the post's author_id. |
| company_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References COMPANIES.company_id; the tagged employer. |
| reviewer_id | INT UNSIGNED | Conditional | FK | References USERS.user_id; the authorized company representative. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED. |
| reviewed_at | DATETIME | Conditional | — | Time the representative approved or rejected the request. |
| showcase | BOOLEAN | Yes | — | Whether approved work is selected for the company showcase. |

### Verification rules

- The requesting student must own the referenced post:
  student_id must equal POSTS.author_id.
- A company is required for this verification workflow.
- Only an authorized representative of that company may approve
  or reject the request.
- reviewer_id and reviewed_at are NULL while pending and required
  after a decision.
- A company tag alone does not mean the work is verified.
- Only APPROVED requests may display a verified indicator.
- showcase may be TRUE only for approved work.
- Proposed default for showcase: FALSE.

Unique post_id allows zero or one current request per post.

**This one-current-request restriction is a design assumption requiring
team approval, not an explicit original functional requirement.**

Foreign keys alone do not enforce student ownership or reviewer
authorization; those rules need additional validation.

## 9. OPPORTUNITIES

Stores jobs and internships offered by employers.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| job_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique opportunity ID. |
| company_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References COMPANIES.company_id. |
| recruiter_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References USERS.user_id; the creating recruiter. |
| title | VARCHAR(150) | Yes | — | Position title. |
| description | TEXT | Yes | — | Responsibilities and requirements. |
| location | VARCHAR(150) | No | — | Work location or remote arrangement. |
| type | VARCHAR(30) | Yes | — | Proposed: JOB or INTERNSHIP. |
| deadline | DATE | No | — | Application deadline, if specified. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: DRAFT, OPEN, or CLOSED. |

Each opportunity belongs to one company and records one creating
recruiter. The application must confirm the recruiter is authorized
to act for that company.

## 10. INVITATIONS

Stores a recruiter's invitation asking a student to apply.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| invitation_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique invitation ID. |
| recruiter_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK | References USERS.user_id; the sender. |
| student_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK + UQ pair | References USERS.user_id; the recipient. |
| job_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK + UQ pair | References OPPORTUNITIES.job_id. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: SENT, ACCEPTED, DECLINED, or EXPIRED. |
| sent_at | DATETIME | Yes | — | Time the invitation was sent. |

Unique combination: (student_id, job_id).

This is a design decision allowing one current invitation per
student/opportunity pair. Reinvitation policy requires team confirmation.

An invitation is not an application. Accepting an invitation does not
automatically mean an application has been submitted.

## 11. APPLICATIONS

Stores a student's submission to an opportunity.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| application_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK | Unique application ID. |
| student_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK + UQ pair | References USERS.user_id; the applicant. |
| job_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | FK + UQ pair | References OPPORTUNITIES.job_id. |
| status | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | — | Proposed: SUBMITTED, UNDER_REVIEW, INTERVIEW, REJECTED, or OFFERED. |
| submitted_at | DATETIME | Yes | — | Time the application was submitted. |

Unique combination: (student_id, job_id).

This is a design decision preventing duplicate applications to the same
opportunity. Reapplication policy requires team confirmation.

A student may apply without receiving an invitation.
The design does not store a direct invitation-to-application link.

## 12. APPLICATION_POSTS

Connects applications to selected portfolio posts.

| Field | Proposed type | Required? | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| application_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References APPLICATIONS.application_id. |
| post_id | INT UNSIGNED | Yes | PK + FK | References POSTS.post_id. |

Composite primary key: (application_id, post_id).

An application can include multiple portfolio posts. A post can be used
in multiple applications. The same pairing cannot appear twice.

The application must verify that each selected post belongs to the
applicant. Company verification is not required for every application
post by the original requirements.

## Shared implementation notes

- Generate single-column ID primary keys automatically.
- Proposed timestamp defaults use the current date and time.
- Agree on email and skill-name case handling before implementation.
- Foreign keys prove referenced records exist; they do not prove
  the user has the appropriate role or permission.
- Required fields, allowed values, status transitions, deletion behavior,
  and the stated design assumptions need team confirmation.

## Scope limitations

This dictionary matches the simplified 12-table core ERD.

Messaging, notifications, social interactions, advisor feedback,
candidate lists, moderation, analytics, configurable permissions,
extra application file attachments, and full decision history are
deferred or simplified.

It does not claim that every feature in the original functional
requirements is supported or implemented.
